Then "nearby" means the wrong thing to you.  "Nearby" means "on
the same level" with no detail whatsoever inside the level.  You
could be one square away from the door of the shop or the entire
distance of the level away from the door of the shop and it
doesn't matter in the least.

> > Your chances of finding something that is there, are at worst 1/7-
> > that means that the chances of not finding it while searching
> > 100 times are about 1 in 5,000,000.

A table of percentages by number of repeat times would be
interesting.  1-in-7 chance each "s".  So the table of
chances of not finding it is (6/7)^N in N tries:

1 - 85.7%
2 - 73.5%
3 - 63.0%
4 - 54.0%
5 - 46.3%
6 - 39.7%
7 - 34.0%
8 - 29.1%
9 - 25.0%

It doesn't drop off all that fast.  No wonder I prefer to risk
kicking or use a stethoscope or wand if one is available.  No
wonder I think a ring is so much better to automatically search
every adjacent square every time without extra effort.  No
wonder I think a blessed +5 rustproof Excalibur wins the search
race.  (2/7)^N in N tries:

1 - 28.6%
2 - 08.2%
3 - 02.3%

By the time you get your strength to 18/** the average of your
stats is high enough that kicking approaches that level of
chances, but before you max your strength it could be around
50% per kick or even less.  Still better than "s" but at a
large cost in health.

Searching strategy with a wand - zap once in each room. zap
once at the end of each corridor.  zap once at every 3rd
square in dark corridors.  Likely done before you need to
resort to the dark corridor sequence.

Searching strategy with a stethescope - apply once in every
direction to every wall and corridor.  Done.

Searching strategy with well enchanted Excalibur - "s" once
in every location at every wall and corridor.  Repeat if you
hit the 2.3% roll.  Done.

Searching strategy with kicking - kick once in every direction
at every wall and corridor.  Search while waiting for your
legs to heal but return to your kicking location when they do.
Lather rinse repeat until dead, may take much longer with a
unihorn.

Searching strategy with a ring - cycle the edges of the
entire level, lather rinse repeat until dead.  Let the ring
do the searching for you leaving you able to try for food
while it works.

Searching strategy with just "s" - 3s at every location to
get to 75% success at every location given that you end up
doing 9 searches of each square from the adjacent search
function.  Use prayer to avoid starvation because you don't
have time to scavenge for food.

> > Also, be aware the searching searches the squares around you,
> > so just being in the room is not enough.

Very important point: "s" searches the *adjacent* squares only.
It shows *nothing* farther than adjacent.

